# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Periergia environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. The app runs WITHOUT any of
# these set — it falls back to in-memory seed data + structured
# placeholder content so you can develop the full loop offline.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude — powers content, quiz, and open-answer grading.
# Without it, the app serves rich placeholder content instead.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (defaults to claude-opus-4-8).
PERIERGIA_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# Supabase — stable syllabus tree + generated-content/quiz cache + media.
# Without these, the app uses the in-memory store (seed.ts) and an in-process
# cache. With them: run supabase/schema.sql, then `npm run seed` to load the
# tree into Postgres. The store (src/lib/store.ts) then reads the tree and
# reads/writes the cache from Postgres — no other code changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Service-role key (server-only — used by API routes to write the cache).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Amazon Associates tag — monetizes the "Further Reading" book lists: each book
# citation gets a tagged "Find it ↗" affiliate link (journal papers and
# author-less reference works are skipped) plus the required disclosure. It
# defaults to our live Associates ID in src/lib/affiliate.ts, so leaving this
# UNSET keeps monetization ON. Override it here to use a different tag, or set
# it to an empty string to turn affiliate links off. Public by design (it rides
# in every affiliate URL); inlined at build time, so redeploy after changing.
# This is the NORTH-AMERICA tag ("-20"): amazon.com / .ca / .com.mx, and the
# rest-of-world fallback.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AMAZON_TAG=

# Amazon Associates UK/EU tag ("-21") — used when a reader is in the UK or EU;
# they're routed to their local Amazon (amazon.co.uk/.de/.fr/.it/.es/…) with
# this tag, since a tag only earns on the marketplace it belongs to. Defaults to
# our live "-21" id. Empty string = no Amazon link for UK/EU readers.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AMAZON_TAG_EU=

# Bookshop.org affiliate id (numeric) — adds a second "Bookshop ↗" link to each
# book alongside Amazon (Bookshop pays 10% and supports indie stores; US/UK
# only). No default: leave UNSET and only Amazon links show. Set it to turn
# Bookshop links on. Public by design; inlined at build, so redeploy to apply.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKSHOP_ID=
